<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_ScaldFloorFauna.xml                 TerminalBiomes — authored 2026-09-26
  ==========================================================================
  SEA_FISHABLES_ALIVE_IN_DEPTHS_1, the SCALD portion. Owner ruling
  2026-09-26: *every* entry in a sea's fishTypes owes a LIVING counterpart
  swimming that sea, not just a catch item — "a catch item on its own is
  half a species."

  ⚠️ NOTHING HERE WAS INVENTED. Each species below was already written, in
  full, inside its own catch item's description (Defs/ThingDefs_Items/
  RUT_ScaldFish.xml, RM_ScaldCatch.xml) — body, size, what it eats, where on
  the crater it lives, how it moves. That prose is the design authority for
  these defs; the descriptions here are the same creature seen alive instead
  of in the pail, and every number is read off the body the item text
  already describes. The item's own spec says this outright: "Author the
  ThingDef + PawnKindDef from the existing item description, not from
  scratch."

  ── the pairing, after this file ──────────────────────────────────────────
  Nine catch entries in RM_TheScald.fishTypes, nine living residents:

    RM_EeshCatch      <-> RM_Eesh        (new here)
    RM_DossCatch      <-> RM_Doss        (new here)
    RM_MuddalCatch    <-> RM_Muddal      (new here)
    RM_ThuumCatch     <-> RM_Thuum       (new here)
    RM_KarrashCatch   <-> RM_Karrash     (new here)
    RM_EkkelCatch     <-> RM_Ekkel       (new here)
    RM_BladderboilCatch <-> RM_Bladderboil (new here)
    RM_ShullaCatch    <-> RM_Shulla      (already shipped, RM_ScaldFauna.xml)
    RM_Saal           <-> RM_Noohm       (already shipped; the one pair whose
                                          two halves carry different species
                                          names on purpose — the catch is
                                          "saal", the living bubble-sailor is
                                          "noohm", per RM_ScaldFauna.xml's own
                                          header)

  ⚠️ SIX CATCH DEFS WERE RENAMED IN THE SAME PASS to make that table
  possible: RM_Eesh/Muddal/Karrash/Doss/Thuum/Ekkel (the ITEMS) became
  RM_*Catch, freeing the bare species name for the animal. That is the
  convention the item's own criteria demand ("Keep the *Catch pairing
  convention") and the one the rest of the project already uses
  (RM_Essarn/RM_EssarnCatch in the Grey Sea; RM_Shulla/RM_ShullaCatch here).
  Call sites updated in the same commit: RM_TheScald.xml fishTypes,
  RUT_RareScaldCatches.xml, scald_showcase.py, and the texture folders.
  The frozen RUT_ tier twin (src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/.../RUT_ScaldFish.xml)
  uses RUT_ defNames throughout and is untouched — no collision either way.

  ── tier ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Every name here is INVENTED, not canon Star Wars, so every def is RM_ and
  ships inline in the franchise-free mod — biome_mod_architecture.md §7 Q11a
  ("Star Wars style naming is NOT Star Wars IP"). That is also why
  RM_Bladderboil is RM_ and not the RUT_Bladderboil its own commission
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/creatures/RUT_hydrocarbon_ecology_commission.md
  §10) wrote down: that document predates both the tier split and Q11a, its
  catch half already shipped into this mod as RM_BladderboilCatch, and a
  bladderboil is the owner's own coinage rather than anything from the
  franchise. Nothing else about §10's design is changed — the name, the
  player-facing description, bodySize ~0.3, loose kettle-fleets and minimal
  MoveSpeed are all taken from it verbatim.

  ── the hard bans (the_scald.md §6), checked one by one ───────────────────
  Ban 1 (never potable): nothing here is a drink route.
  Ban 2 (never the terminator seas' biome): every def is RM_Scald-side and
        referenced only from RM_TheScald; none is shared with RM_GreySea or
        RM_TwilightSea.
  Ban 3 (no boiling-immune traversal for free): these are the water's OWN
        life, not a route a colonist can wear. Ban 3 governs what the PLAYER
        can cross for nothing; scald_steam_and_hazards_spec.md §1 states the
        distinction outright ("Native immunity is not traversal-for-free").
  Ban 4 (no macro-life in the boil itself): honoured, and worth stating per
        species because it is the ban most easily broken here. Nothing below
        is macro-life. The three vent/margin dwellers (karrash, ekkel,
        muddal) live ON the chimneys and mats, the two shoal feeders (eesh,
        doss) work the column and the dung-fall, thuum lives UNDER the mats,
        and the bladderboil is written into the ban's own carve-out
        ("nothing swims the roiling surface layer but bubbles and sails") by
        its own commission §10b: it does not swim the boil, it floats it —
        it IS its own bubble, the sail register's second member.
  Ban 5 (no drained, cooled or tamed Scald): no def here changes terrain,
        and every one is trainability None — nothing here tames.
  Ban 6 (no vanilla-Earth flora or fauna): every species is invented and
        described as its own thing. Where a real-world word appears in the
        prose it is a resemblance ("crab-thing", "shrimp-thing"), never an
        identification — the same de-Earthing the Grey Deep's rimshell uses.

  ── mechanically plain, on purpose ────────────────────────────────────────
  No C#, no comps beyond the vanilla animal shape, pattern copied from
  RM_ScaldFauna.xml's own two residents (which in turn copy
  RSW_SandStalker.xml's placeholder idiom). Every one takes
  RM_OrganicScaldNative with Inherit="False" — that is RM_ScaldFauna.xml's
  standing file-header rule ("every Scald native takes RM_OrganicScaldNative")
  and without it HediffGiver_Terrain burns them alive in the water they are
  made of. foodType is OmnivoreAnimal throughout even where the fiction is a
  grazer: the crowncarpet mats they eat are gated behind a terrain tag that
  a given map may not carry, and a VegetarianAnimal with no plants starves.

  ── art ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Placeholder silhouettes at each texPath, three facings each, real art
  filed to the artpipe in the same pass (scaldfloor_*). Checked first, per
  the standing rule: no existing render in done/ or _artsrc/ covers any of
  these seven — the only Scald creature art that exists is noohm and shulla,
  both already wired.

  ── design gaps found while building, NOT resolved here ───────────────────
  * eesh and shulla are written as the same creature. Both are "the silver
    shoal", both hot-white slivers darting in company between the vent
    plumes, both feeding the dung-fall. They ship as two species with two
    catch items and two roster rows. This is a content question for the
    owner (merge, or differentiate one of them), not a build decision, and
    nothing here pre-empts it: both are authored faithfully to their own
    text.
  * RUT_BladderboilBladder (the commission's §14c butchery product) is not
    built. It needs the pawn to exist first, which it now does.
  ==========================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- =================================================================
       RM_Eesh — the silver of the Scald. Tiny, finless, mirror-skinned;
       lives in the boiling column, feeds on the dung-fall of the herds
       below. Its catch item is the one thing on the crater people call
       delicious without a caveat.
       ================================================================= -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Eesh</defName>
    <label>eesh</label>
    <description>A finger-long, finless sliver with no scales at all — the skin is a heat-mirror, and it lives in the boiling column itself, hanging in the rising water where nothing else will go. They move as one cloud and never alone; a shoal turning is a flash you can see from the rim. They are eating, constantly, whatever settles down out of the water above them.</description>
